Later the same Saturday, we got very busy again.
A young woman came up to the counter and ordered a large cappuccino.
Now I had made many cappuccinos.
My first cups were not quite perfect.
But this time I was ready.
I took the metal pitcher and poured cold milk into it.
I placed the pitcher under the machine and turned on the hot steam.
I have practiced a lot since I started.
I did not turn up the pressure immediately.
I have actually learned to listen to the machine.
The loud sound from the steam was exactly right this time.
The milk slowly became warm.
And the foam on top became very thick and soft.
It was a big step forward.
I carefully poured the milk over the coffee in a large cup.
It actually looked like a real professional cappuccino.
"Here you go," I said and placed the cup on the counter.
The woman smiled and took her coffee.
I have finally learned to control the pressure.
